cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use peyesim, please cite it as below. peyesim is a Python port of the
  R package eyesim; please also cite the methods you use (for example
  MultiMatch, Dewhurst et al., 2012).
type: software
title: "peyesim: analysis of eye-movement data in Python"
abstract: >-
  Fixation density maps, template similarity with permutation baselines,
  MultiMatch scanpath comparison, cross-recurrence analysis and revisitation
  scoring for eye-movement data. A Python port of the R package eyesim.
authors:
  - family-names: Buchsbaum
    given-names: Bradley
    email: brad.buchsbaum@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bbuchsbaum/peyesim"
url: "https://bbuchsbaum.github.io/peyesim/"
keywords:
  - eye tracking
  - eye movements
  - scanpath
  - MultiMatch
  - gaze reinstatement
references:
